  "goodToKnow": "Das Konzentrationslager (KZ) is a concentration camp. The Nazis opened Dachau in 1933 for political opponents; later the system included Buchenwald, Sachsenhausen and Bergen-Belsen, and extermination camps like Auschwitz-Birkenau and Treblinka, where millions of Jews and others were murdered. Since 1996, 27 January, the day Auschwitz was liberated in 1945, has been Germany's day of remembrance. Many camps are now memorials. Plural: die Konzentrationslager."
